.TH "Keepmenu" "1" "22 August 2026" "Keepmenu 1.6.0" "User Manual"
.SH NAME
keepmenu \- Fully featured Dmenu/Rofi frontend for autotype and managing
of Keepass databases.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]keepmenu\f[R] [\f[B]\(enautotype\f[R] pattern]
[\f[B]\(enconfig\f[R] file] [\f[B]\(enclipboard\f[R]]
[\f[B]\(endatabase\f[R] file] [\f[B]\(enkeyfile\f[R] file]
[\f[B]\(enlock\f[R]] [\f[B]\(enno\-prompt\f[R]] [\f[B]\(enshow\f[R]
term] [\f[B]\(enfield\f[R] name] [\f[B]\(entotp\f[R]]
[\f[B]\(enversion\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\f[B]Keepmenu\f[R] is a fast and minimal application to facilitate
password entry and manage most aspects of Keepass .kdbx databases.
It is inspired in part by Passhole, but is more dmenu and less command
line focused.
.PP
With \f[B]\(enshow\f[R] it also works as a CLI\-only password manager,
requiring only Pykeepass.
.SH OPTIONS
\f[B]\-a\f[R], \f[B]\(enautotype\f[R] Autotype sequence from
https://keepass.info/help/base/autotype.html#autoseq .
Overrides global default from config.ini for current database.
.PP
\f[B]\-c\f[R], \f[B]\(enconfig\f[R] Path to config file
.PP
\f[B]\-C\f[R], \f[B]\(enclipboard\f[R] Select to clipboard
.PP
\f[B]\-d\f[R], \f[B]\(endatabase\f[R] Path to Keepass database
.PP
\f[B]\-f\f[R], \f[B]\(enfield\f[R] Field to output with
\f[B]\(enshow\f[R].
Repeat for multiple fields, which are output one per line in the order
given.
One of \f[I]title\f[R], \f[I]username\f[R], \f[I]password\f[R],
\f[I]url\f[R], \f[I]notes\f[R], \f[I]totp\f[R],
\f[CR]S:<attribute>\f[R], or \f[I]all\f[R] for every field that has a
value, labeled.
Defaults to \f[I]password\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\(enhelp\f[R] Print help and exit
.PP
\f[B]\-k\f[R], \f[B]\(enkeyfile\f[R] Path to keyfile
.PP
\f[B]\-l\f[R], \f[B]\(enlock\f[R] Lock all open databases and stop the
keepmenu daemon.
.PP
\f[B]\-n\f[R], \f[B]\(enno\-prompt\f[R] Do not prompt for database
password
.PP
\f[B]\-s\f[R], \f[B]\(enshow\f[R] Search term(s).
Outputs the matched entry\(cqs password (default) or the fields selected
by \f[B]\(enfield\f[R] to stdout or to the clipboard with
\f[B]\(enclipboard\f[R].
Requires a single matching entry
.PP
\f[B]\-t\f[R], \f[B]\(entotp\f[R] TOTP mode
.PP
\f[B]\-V\f[R], \f[B]\(enversion\f[R] Show version and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
keepmenu
keepmenu \-t
keepmenu \-c /etc/keepmenu/config.ini
keepmenu \-d \(ti/docs/totp_passwords.kdbx \-a \(aq{TOTP}{ENTER}\(aq
keepmenu \-d \(ti/passwords.kdbx \-k \(ti/passwords.keyfile \-a \(aq{S:security question}{ENTER}\(aq
keepmenu \-s \(dqproduction/ssh db\(dq \-d \(ti/passwords.kdbx
keepmenu \-s \(dqproduction/ssh db\(dq \-d \(ti/passwords.kdbx \-f username \-f password
keepmenu \-l
.EE
.SH CONFIGURATION
If you start keepmenu for the first time without a config file, it will
prompt you for database and keyfile locations and save them in a default
config file.
.PP
OR Copy config.ini.example to \(ti/.config/keepmenu/config.ini and use
it as a reference for additional options.
.PP
Alternatively you can specify the file path to your config.ini using the
\-c/\(enconfig flag.
.SS config.ini options and defaults
.PP
